# CODEOWNERS — GDF repo root (v1.2, GDF-012).
# The workflow states its own path must be protected: a validator a PR can weaken in the same PR is
# not a validator. GDF's OVR-1 grants AGENTS merge authority to protected branches — so the paths
# that BOUND that authority are the ones that must never be agent-editable.
# An unfilled CODEOWNERS silently protects nothing; every entry names a real account.

*                             @umutcanapaydin

# The enforcement surface — the paths an agent could use to disarm its own bounds.
/.github/                     @umutcanapaydin
/.governed-records            @umutcanapaydin
/scripts/                     @umutcanapaydin
/schemas/                     @umutcanapaydin
/conformance/                 @umutcanapaydin
/.secret-scan-allow           @umutcanapaydin   # a bypass surface: adding a literal is a security decision

# The constitution and the decision trail.
/GDF-CONSTITUTION.md          @umutcanapaydin
/decisions.md                 @umutcanapaydin
/permission-matrix.md         @umutcanapaydin
